-- DRC
('Pondu', 'DRC', 'Africa', true, 'Dinner', 'pondu-drc',
'Congolese cassava leaf stew slow-cooked with palm oil and smoked fish - the DRC''s national dinner.',
'Pondu (also called Saka Saka) is the Democratic Republic of Congo''s most eaten dish. The cassava leaves are pounded and cooked for hours, creating a uniquely rich, dark stew.',
'Medium', 30, 90, 6, ARRAY['dinner', 'congolese', 'cassava', 'palm-oil', 'national-dish'],
'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512058564366-18510be2db19?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop',
'[{"item":"Cassava leaves","quantity":"500g","note":"ground"},{"item":"Palm oil","quantity":"1/3 cup"},{"item":"Smoked fish","quantity":"200g"},{"item":"Onion","quantity":"1","note":"chopped"},{"item":"Tomatoes","quantity":"2","note":"diced"},{"item":"Eggplant","quantity":"1","note":"diced"},{"item":"Garlic","quantity":"3 cloves"},{"item":"Chili pepper","quantity":"1"},{"item":"Salt","quantity":"to taste"},{"item":"Fufu","quantity":"for serving"}]',
'[{"step":1,"instruction":"Boil ground cassava leaves for 30 minutes. Drain."},{"step":2,"instruction":"Heat palm oil. Sauté onion, garlic, and tomatoes."},{"step":3,"instruction":"Add cassava leaves, eggplant, and smoked fish."},{"step":4,"instruction":"Add 1 cup water and whole chili. Simmer on low heat for 45-60 minutes."},{"step":5,"instruction":"Serve with fufu (cassava flour dough)."}]'),

('Chikwanga', 'DRC', 'Africa', true, 'Lunch', 'chikwanga-drc',
'Congolese fermented cassava bread wrapped and steamed in banana leaves - dense and satisfying.',
'Chikwanga is a traditional Congolese bread made from fermented cassava. The banana leaf wrapping imparts a subtle flavor and keeps it moist for days.',
'Medium', 480, 60, 6, ARRAY['lunch', 'congolese', 'cassava', 'fermented', 'bread'],
'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574484284002-952d92456975?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop',
'[{"item":"Cassava","quantity":"2 kg","note":"peeled"},{"item":"Banana leaves","quantity":"for wrapping"},{"item":"Water","quantity":"for soaking"},{"item":"Salt","quantity":"1 tsp"}]',
'[{"step":1,"instruction":"Soak peeled cassava in water for 3-5 days until soft and fermented."},{"step":2,"instruction":"Drain and pound into a smooth, elastic dough."},{"step":3,"instruction":"Shape into logs. Wrap tightly in banana leaves."},{"step":4,"instruction":"Steam wrapped chikwanga for 45-60 minutes until firm."},{"step":5,"instruction":"Serve sliced with pondu or any stew."}]'),

-- CAMEROON
('Eru', 'Cameroon', 'Africa', true, 'Dinner', 'eru-cameroon',
'Cameroonian wild spinach and waterleaf stew with crayfish and palm oil - a South West Region specialty.',
'Eru is the pride of Cameroon''s South West and North West regions. The wild eru leaves are hand-shredded into hair-thin strips, a labor-intensive process that creates the dish''s signature texture.',
